o_compilation() {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/guest_pipeline.rs:407:#[test]\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/guest_pipeline.rs:408:fn loader_inheritance_survives_orchestration_environment_purge() {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:10:    fn archive(name: &str, kind: tar::EntryType, bytes: &[u8]) -> Vec<u8> {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:21:    fn payload() -> Vec<u8> {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:24:    fn pins(payload: &[u8]) -> Pins {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:27:    fn fake(root: &Path, payload: &[u8]) -> Result<PathBuf> {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:33:    fn cache(root: &Path) -> PathBuf {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:36:    fn destination(root: &Path) -> PathBuf {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:39:    fn cleaned(root: &Path) {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:47:    fn hash_before_parse_and_exact_regular_member_before_publication() {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:81:    fn symlinks_in_every_component_including_dangling_are_refused() {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:111:    fn partial_wrong_and_nonregular_installations_never_download() {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:132:    fn malicious_lock_types_refuse_without_following_or_blocking() {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:151:    fn download_failure_cleans_private_staging_and_never_publishes() {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:166:    fn concurrent_installers_publish_once_and_return_same_path() {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:221:    fn native_curl_contract_and_download_failure_cleanup() {\nmodel/dev/xtask/tests/apalache/cases.rs:278:    fn native_dispatch_usage_failure_is_nonzero_and_structured() {\n# Native identity control ownership\n\nThe owner says “feel free to make breaking changes from pytjon driver” and “we don't need backwards compatabiltiy” (2026-10-24; parent spec Conversation Evidence). These native controls retain behavior rather than Python bytes. Integration target: `cargo test -p xtask --test guest_identity --locked`.\n\n| Retained Python control | Native Rust control in tests/identity |\n| --- | --- |\n| lock: unrelated workspace packages/dev exclusions | lock::unrelated_and_dev_only_dependencies_do_not_change_guest_closures |\n| lock: workspace unified optional edges | lock::unified_edges_and_edge_topology_change_ancestor_identity |\n| lock: checkout portability | lock::content_addressed_publication_is_repeatable_and_portable |\n| lock: checksum propagation to every dependent | lock::checksum_changes_propagate_through_normal_and_all_platform_build_edges |\n| lock: all-platform build dependencies | same table-driven checksum/edge control |\n| lock: edge topology | lock::unified_edges_and_edge_topology_change_ancestor_identity |\n| lock: ambiguous name/version sources | lock::ambiguous_name_version_coordinates_are_marked_unavailable |\n| lock: missing sourced lock entry / git checksum optional | lock::sourced_entries_are_required_but_git_checksums_are_optional |\n| lock: CLI publication / malformed document | lock::content_addressed_publication_is_repeatable_and_portable; lock::malformed_native_documents_and_graphs_are_rejected; actual CLI metadata evidence |\n| rustc: portable host metadata/path identity | compiler::portable_identity_replaces_guest_metadata_and_remaps_generated_paths |\n| rustc: dependency identity propagation | compiler::dependency_identity_and_transitive_variants_propagate |\n| rustc: package/version/features/profile/compiler/lock distinctions | compiler::package_features_profile_compiler_and_closure_remain_distinct |\n| rustc: missing/ambiguous closure | compiler::missing_ambiguous_and_malformed_lock_maps_refuse |\n| rustc: build-std exemption and refusals | compiler::build_std_requires_wasm_marker_and_trusted_source_or_rust_src_coordinate |\n| rustc: missing/corrupt sidecar | compiler::invalid_or_missing_dependency_sidecars_and_macro_collisions_refuse |\n| rustc: portable native macro without argv rewriting | compiler::native_macro_identity_ignores_host_configuration_but_retains_argv_and_collisions |\n| rustc: native macro collision | compiler::invalid_or_missing_dependency_sidecars_and_macro_collisions_refuse |\n| rustc: probe passthrough | compiler::probes_pass_through_without_guest_environment |\n| rustc: compiler failure cleanup | compiler::sidecar_precedes_child_and_cleanup_preserves_exit_launch_and_signal_outcomes |\n| rustc: pipelined metadata availability | same lifecycle control; native compiler fixture reads the sidecar before exit |\n| rustc: inherited jobserver FD | compiler::inherited_jobserver_descriptor_reaches_direct_compiler_child |\n\nAdditional native controls cover raw OS argv/environment bytes and lexical root boundaries; previous-wrapper ordering and loader environment; launch failure and signal status; actual dependency-free rustc proc-macro compilation in two checkout roots; malformed options/required inputs; sorted JSON and a known SHA-256 vector; concurrent atomic publication, rename-failure temporary cleanup, and serialized sidecar cleanup; current Cargo/mise/toolchain/rust-src TOML.\n\nExplicitly retired under the owner amendment: Python import fixtures/interpreter launchers, shebang copying and Python-executable whitespace restrictions, Python exception names/text, json.dumps spaces/escaping/order, exact old hashes and schema-1 JSON. Native JSON is schema 2; serde_json/toml own grammar/errors/resource limits. No Python BigInt, date, NaN, recursion, digit, Unicode or diagnostic-order emulation is recreated. Paths with spaces and non-UTF-8 Unix bytes remain useful controls.\n\nThe retained Python helpers are unchanged and still serve current shell callers. Task .5 replaces their active invocation and invalidates schema-1 caches. Final task .3 wires the canonical workspace stage once and owns full integrated guest reproduction/freshness plus TLC/Apalache validation. No frozen artifact or guest bytes changed here. Linux evidence does not claim native macOS execution; loader bytes are exercised on the available host.\nPorted retired-name filtering to native xtask and switched the shell caller to the compiled tool. Removed the byte-only original-artifact verifier, its active manifest and Python call while preserving the independent lifecycle comparison and changed-edge mutation control.\n\nTier: session (jev-unavailable(no_key)), roleimplementer gpt-6.1-sol medium.\nstage: impl-review - skipped(policy: parallel-wave - conductor owns the gate)\n\nStatus: in_progress; conductor owns integration, review and Flow completion.\nWorkspace: /Users/stephan/Workspace/skunkworks/umpire/temporal/.worktrees/fn2477-port\nCommit: e4899e270f\nBaseline: green (old Python policy control; existing xtask tests; two compatibility controls). No Flow CLI was called, per conductor's shared-state freeze.\n\nControls and evidence:\n- `raw_records_exempt_only_author_facade_tokens`: raw NUL path/number/line records, newline-bearing/non-UTF8 paths and lines, trailing EOF, exact exemption boundaries and mixed forbidden/exempt tokens.\n- `malformed_records_fail_closed`: missing separators, empty/nondecimal line numbers return 2.\n- `posix_ere_recheck_and_grep_failure_propagate`: external POSIX character classes, invalid ERE status 2; no Rust-regex substitution.\n- `active_spellings_and_historical_exclusions`: Rust counterpart of the removed Python policy test's active spelling matrix, allowed current names, global historical exclusions and narrower layout-only exclusions.\n- `tool_failures_never_report_clean`: git error 7, malformed git stream 2, grep error 9 never report clean.\n- `io_and_missing_grep_errors_fail_closed`: output failure and missing grep return 2.\n- Compatibility selector executes exactly two fixture tests: `retained_original_exact_lifecycle_projection` and unchanged `changed_original_lifecycle_edge_fails_the_same_comparison`. Both pass. Original snapshots and historical hash artifacts have no diff.\n- Initial native corpus: 3 failed with absent-command diagnostics before implementation; final corpus: 6 passed. The full baseline xtask suite passed. Final xtask clippy all-targets passed. Final real repository scan using the built binary returned 0.\n\nNative contract amendment (owner 2026-10-24): Python Unicode whitespace classification is retired in favor of documented byte/ASCII token boundaries. Exact Python traceback/diagnostic bytes and checksum-only original verification are retired. Raw non-UTF8 data is preserved, not lossily decoded. Grep children are waited even after input write failure; successful early grep exit may close its input pipe.\n\nIntegration obligations: shell uses `helper=$(bash \"$workspace/scripts/xtask.sh\")` once before scanning, with UMPIRE_XTASK absolute binary override for focused controls. Lane .5 owns the shared bootstrap file, absent from this lane by agreement. Conductor must join dispatcher/lib/caller edits and run standalone bootstrap, filter, lifecycle and mutation controls against integrated source before marking done. No canonical guest publication or full Model gate was run here.\n\nLogs (workspace-relative): .flow/tmp/fn2477-baseline.log, fn2477-red.log, fn2477-green.log, fn2477-verify.log, fn2477-final2.log, fn2477-shell-final.log. Intermediate clippy style failures are retained in fn2477-verify.log and fn2477-final.log; final2 is green. All commands completed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
